{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Your name is Jacob.</b> He says: for now you are still called Jacob, even though he changed your name to the sar of Esav, for he was not sent to you to change your name. But from now on your name shall no longer be called Jacob, but rather Israel shall be your name. And this is the meaning of \"and He called his name Israel.\" Or he may hint that He called his name Israel in addition to Jacob, not that it is forbidden to be called Jacob."], :book "genesis", :voice :ramban, :lang :pt, :chapter 35, :timestamp "2026-07-27T15:17:46.772644264Z", :translated-from :en, :model "glm-5.2"}